(window.GROUP_QUIZZES=window.GROUP_QUIZZES||{})["intro-to-pa-profession-pa-intro-master-exam-form-e"]={"title":"Intro to PA Profession Comprehensive Master Exam — Form E","category":"Intro to PA","questions":[{"q":"The physician was historically considered the 'captain of the ship,' with care regarded as the:","choices":["Silver standard","Gold standard","Platinum standard","Bronze standard"],"answer":1,"exp":"The physician was historically viewed as the \"captain of the ship,\" and physician-delivered care was regarded as the gold standard against which new provider roles were measured. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"Which provider category is described as an important 'stop-gap measure' in several countries' healthcare systems?","choices":["Nurse anesthetists","Hospital administrators","Community pharmacists","Physician substitutes"],"answer":3,"exp":"Physician substitutes are described as an important \"stop-gap measure\" used in several countries to address physician shortages created by war, revolution, or other social/political turmoil. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"Dr. Stead's envisioned provider would work closely with physicians and importantly not:","choices":["Treat patients","Document care","Threaten them","Earn a salary"],"answer":2,"exp":"Dr. Stead envisioned a provider working closely with physicians in a role between nurse and doctor that would not threaten physicians -- a key design principle behind the earliest PA concept. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"The first Duke PA program was NOT initially intended to have any role in:","choices":["Direct patient contact","Taking patient histories","Charting patient notes","Diagnosing or prescribing"],"answer":3,"exp":"The first Duke PA program was not initially intended to include diagnosing or prescribing -- the earliest corpsmen were trained for a more limited technical role, with independent medical decision-making added only later as the profession matured. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"Which stage is marked by 'steady growth and acceptance' and 'inclusion into recognized workforce supply'?","choices":["Evaluation phase","Incorporation","Ideology stage","Maturation stage"],"answer":1,"exp":"Incorporation is the stage marked by steady growth and acceptance, including expanded utilization beyond the profession's original scope and formal inclusion in the recognized workforce supply through regulation and reimbursement. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"Consolidation issues in the maturation era include supply concerns, resident work-hour changes, name change, and:","choices":["Accreditation","Licensure exams","Certification","Autonomy/OTP"],"answer":3,"exp":"Autonomy and Optimal Team Practice (OTP) round out the consolidation issues of the maturation era, alongside supply concerns, resident work-hour changes, and the name change. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"Dr. Charles Hudson, who introduced the PA concept, was president of which organization?","choices":["NBME","AMA","AAPA","NCCPA"],"answer":0,"exp":"Dr. Charles Hudson, who first introduced the PA concept in a 1961 speech to the AMA House of Delegates, was president of the NBME (National Board of Medical Examiners) at the time. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"Which program model came from the University of Washington?","choices":["Feldsher","Medex","Type A","Child Health Associate"],"answer":1,"exp":"The Medex model came from Dr. Richard Smith at the University of Washington. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"In 1984, the AAPA achieved which milestone?","choices":["First female president elected","Name change to Physician Associate","Launch of the PANRE exam","Creation of the first CAQ"],"answer":0,"exp":"In 1984, the AAPA elected its first female president, a milestone in the organization's leadership history. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"The first National PA Day was celebrated in what year?","choices":["1987","1992","1981","1975"],"answer":0,"exp":"The first National PA Day was celebrated in 1987. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"In 1995, the US State Department began hiring PAs as:","choices":["Uniformed federal law enforcement officers","Civilian medical research consultants","Career diplomatic corps ambassadors","Foreign Service health practitioners"],"answer":3,"exp":"In 1995, the US State Department began hiring PAs as Foreign Service health practitioners, extending the profession's reach into federal international service. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"By 1990, approximately how many PAs were certified?","choices":["21,194","92,049","201,038","9,431"],"answer":0,"exp":"By 1990, approximately 21,194 PAs were certified, alongside 45 accredited programs. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"The 2011 creation of a Chief PA position occurred at which system?","choices":["Kaiser Permanente Health System","Cleveland Clinic Foundation","Mayo Clinic Health System","Veterans Administration"],"answer":3,"exp":"The Veterans Administration created a Chief PA position in 2011, the same year NCCPA introduced its first CAQs. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"A Certificate of Added Qualifications is abbreviated as:","choices":["CNS","CHA","CAQ","CME"],"answer":2,"exp":"CAQ stands for Certificate of Added Qualifications, the specialty-recognition credential NCCPA offers PAs in areas like emergency medicine, hospital medicine, and orthopaedic surgery. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"The PA History Society preserves memorabilia including coins, pins, T-shirts, and:","choices":["Textbooks","Stethoscopes","Flags","Diplomas"],"answer":2,"exp":"The PA History Society's memorabilia collections include items like coins, pins, T-shirts, and flags, alongside oral histories, biographies, and photos documenting the profession. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — History of the PA Profession"},{"q":"ARC-PA awards accreditation through a process that includes documentation and periodic:","choices":["Program self-surveys","Site visit evaluations","Remote phone interviews","Standardized written exams"],"answer":1,"exp":"ARC-PA's accreditation process includes documentation review as well as periodic site visit evaluations conducted by appointed site visitors. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"A key ARC-PA goal is to foster excellence through uniform national:","choices":["Salaries","Exams","Standards","Curricula only"],"answer":2,"exp":"A key ARC-PA goal is to foster excellence in PA education through uniform national standards that all accredited programs must meet. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"The ARC-PA mission is to protect the interests of the public and the PA:","choices":["Employers","Schools","Profession","Physicians"],"answer":2,"exp":"ARC-PA's mission is to protect the interests of the public and the PA profession by defining and enforcing educational standards. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"PAEA is the national organization representing PA:","choices":["Educational programs","Certified practicing PAs","PA employers and practices","Supervising physicians"],"answer":0,"exp":"PAEA is the national organization representing PA educational programs, administering CASPA and assessment tools like PACKRAT. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"Which designation does NCCPA confer on certified PAs?","choices":["RPA","PA-C","PA-S","MPA"],"answer":1,"exp":"NCCPA confers the PA-C designation on PAs who pass its certifying exam, marking them as nationally certified. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"NCCPA also produces annual reports on the status of:","choices":["PA programs","Physicians","Certified PAs","Nursing programs"],"answer":2,"exp":"NCCPA produces annual reports on the status of certified PAs, tracking the certificant population it oversees. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"Which is a CAQ offered by NCCPA?","choices":["Anesthesiology and Pain Management","Pathology and Laboratory Medicine","Palliative Medicine and Hospice Care","Diagnostic Radiology and Imaging"],"answer":2,"exp":"Palliative Medicine and Hospice Care is one of the CAQs NCCPA offers, alongside specialties like Emergency Medicine, Hospital Medicine, and Orthopaedic Surgery. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"The AAPA mission is to lead the profession and empower members to advance careers and enhance:","choices":["Patient health","Accreditation","Research funding","Member salaries"],"answer":0,"exp":"The AAPA mission is to lead the profession and empower members to advance their careers while enhancing patient health, consistent with its vision of PAs transforming health through patient-centered care. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"How many caucuses are within the AAPA House of Delegates?","choices":["5","15","27","58"],"answer":1,"exp":"The AAPA House of Delegates includes 15 caucuses. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"SAAAPA board committees include Advocacy and Policy, Communication and Outreach, Service, and:","choices":["Leadership and Diversity","Certification and Testing","Finance and Budget","Accreditation and Standards"],"answer":0,"exp":"SAAAPA board committees include Advocacy and Policy, Communication and Outreach, Service, and Leadership and Diversity. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"The PAF vision emphasizes PAs connecting clinical expertise and compassion to:","choices":["Physician oversight","Community need","Research goals","Salary growth"],"answer":1,"exp":"The PAF vision emphasizes PAs connecting clinical expertise and compassion to community need, reflecting the foundation's philanthropic focus. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"FAPA promotes monthly CME events in the form of:","choices":["Webinars only","Online modules","Conferences only","CME dinners"],"answer":3,"exp":"FAPA promotes monthly CME events in the form of CME dinners, in addition to its annual CME conference. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"A student society must be registered with which body for a member to become an AOR rep?","choices":["Accreditation Review Commission","Federation of State Medical Boards","National Certification Commission","Student Academy of the AAPA"],"answer":3,"exp":"A student society must be registered with the Student Academy of the AAPA (SAAAPA) for one of its members to become an AOR representative. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"The PAF Board of Trustees includes how many PA Trustees (including one student)?","choices":["9-12","5-7","15-20","20-25"],"answer":0,"exp":"The PAF Board of Trustees includes roughly 9-12 PA Trustees, including one student trustee. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"Which NCCPA resource lists employment opportunities?","choices":["CASPA Portal","PA Career Center","AAPA Huddle Community","JAAPA Journal Archive"],"answer":1,"exp":"The NCCPA PA Career Center is the NCCPA resource that lists employment opportunities for certified PAs. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PA Organizations"},{"q":"Which PA competency domain includes 'engage the abilities of available health professionals'?","choices":["Person-centered care delivery","Knowledge for clinical practice","Professionalism and ethical practice","Interprofessional collaboration"],"answer":3,"exp":"Interprofessional Collaboration is the PA competency domain that includes engaging the abilities of available health professionals, alongside integrating clinical care with public health. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"A complete list of PA competencies is available on the website of which organizations?","choices":["Only the National Commission on Certification","Only the Accreditation Review Commission","Any of the four national PA organizations","Only the American Academy of Physician Associates"],"answer":2,"exp":"A complete list of PA competencies is available on the website of any of the four national PA organizations, since the competencies were jointly adopted and revised by all four. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"Over half of employers say the PA-C credential affects what?","choices":["Malpractice insurance rates","Institutional salary caps","Weekly work scheduling","Reimbursement decisions"],"answer":3,"exp":"Over half of employers report that the PA-C credential affects their reimbursement decisions, reflecting how payers and employers value NCCPA certification. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"How long is the entire PANCE testing day?","choices":["Six hours","Five hours","Eight hours","Three hours"],"answer":0,"exp":"The entire PANCE testing day runs six hours, structured as six 60-minute blocks of 60 questions each with built-in break time. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"On PANCE test day, candidates are advised to arrive how early?","choices":["2 hours","10 minutes","30 minutes","1 hour"],"answer":2,"exp":"Candidates are advised to arrive 30 minutes early on PANCE test day. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"The name on a candidate's driver's license must match the name on the:","choices":["PA school diploma","Original application","Scheduling permit","CME activity log"],"answer":2,"exp":"The name on a candidate's driver's license must match the name on the scheduling permit presented at check-in. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"The only way to establish new PANCE eligibility after exhausting attempts is to:","choices":["Wait a mandatory ten-year waiting period","Complete a new ARC-PA accredited program","Obtain an unrelated clinical doctoral degree","File a formal appeal directly with NCCPA"],"answer":1,"exp":"After exhausting PANCE attempts, the only way to establish new eligibility is to complete a new ARC-PA accredited PA program. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"Florida PAs are also regulated by the Osteopathic Medical Practice Act numbered:","choices":["456","458.347","459.022","64B8-30"],"answer":2,"exp":"Florida PAs are also regulated under the Osteopathic Medical Practice Act, numbered 459.022. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"A Florida PA license application remains valid for how long?","choices":["6 months","30 days","1 year","2 years"],"answer":2,"exp":"A Florida PA license application remains valid for 1 year. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"Which is a benefit of licensure per the lecture?","choices":["Allows performing/ordering reimbursable services","Permanently exempts PAs from CME requirements","Automatically guarantees full autonomous practice","Fully replaces the need for NCCPA certification"],"answer":0,"exp":"Licensure allows a PA to perform and order reimbursable services, one of its practical benefits beyond simply satisfying a legal requirement to practice. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"Restraint and seclusion orders may NOT be:","choices":["Time-limited","Standing or PRN orders","Face-to-face assessed","Consulted with a physician"],"answer":1,"exp":"Restraint and seclusion orders may not be standing or PRN orders -- they must be specific, time-limited, and based on face-to-face assessment. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"Which best describes a bundled payment for surgery?","choices":["Coverage that excludes all post-operative visits","One payment including pre-op, intra-op, and post-op","Separate itemized bills issued for each visit","A single fee paid only to the operating surgeon"],"answer":1,"exp":"A bundled payment for surgery is a single payment that covers pre-operative, intra-operative, and post-operative services together as one package. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"Which is an example of a value-based care model emphasizing preventive care and chronic disease management?","choices":["A traditional solo private-pay fee schedule","Standard fee-for-service billing arrangements","A cash-only, self-pay private practice model","Medicare Advantage and commercial VBC plans"],"answer":3,"exp":"Medicare Advantage and commercial value-based care plans exemplify VBC models that emphasize preventive care and chronic disease management. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"Medicare Part A covers which services?","choices":["Prescription drugs","Managed care","Outpatient","Hospital services"],"answer":3,"exp":"Medicare Part A covers hospital services. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"Approximately how many Americans are covered by Medicare?","choices":["70 million","50 million","100 million","30 million"],"answer":0,"exp":"Approximately 70 million Americans are covered by Medicare. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"Which best describes 'incident-to' billing?","choices":["Billing that is prohibited under all federal payer rules","PA services hidden and billed at 100% with restrictions","PA services billed directly and visibly at 85 percent","A billing pathway restricted only to surgical procedures"],"answer":1,"exp":"\"Incident-to\" billing describes PA services that are billed under the supervising physician's name at 100% of the physician fee, subject to a number of restrictions, with the PA's role effectively hidden from the claim. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"Students may document in the medical record, but the supervising PA/physician must do what?","choices":["Read, amend if necessary, and sign","Rewrite the entire note from scratch","Disregard the student's note entirely","Delete and replace the student's note"],"answer":0,"exp":"Students may document in the medical record, but the supervising PA or physician must read the note, amend it if necessary, and sign it. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"},{"q":"A key WHO-aligned outcome of interprofessional collaboration is reduced:","choices":["Mortality","Documentation","Reimbursement","Staffing"],"answer":0,"exp":"A key WHO-aligned outcome of interprofessional collaboration is reduced mortality, alongside improved patient compliance and decreased professional burnout. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Health Care is Teamwork"},{"q":"Which nursing provider historically trained via a three-year hospital diploma model?","choices":["CRNA","Clinical nurse specialist","Nurse practitioner","Registered nurse"],"answer":3,"exp":"The registered nurse (RN) is the provider historically trained via a three-year hospital diploma model, before nursing education broadly shifted toward degree-based programs. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Health Care is Teamwork"},{"q":"The shift in nursing education from diploma programs to degree programs led to what critique?","choices":["Lower demand","Degree creep","Reduced theory","Fewer specialties"],"answer":1,"exp":"The shift in nursing education from diploma programs to degree programs led to the critique of \"degree creep\" -- rising credential requirements for entry into the field. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Health Care is Teamwork"},{"q":"A medical assistant typically delivers patient care in which phase?","choices":["After hospital discharge","During surgical anesthesia","Before the examination","During the operation itself"],"answer":2,"exp":"A medical assistant typically delivers patient care before the examination, handling pre-exam tasks alongside clerical duties. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Health Care is Teamwork"},{"q":"An optometrist performs eye exams and prescribes:","choices":["Local anesthesia","Physical therapy","Corrective lenses","Oral antibiotics"],"answer":2,"exp":"An optometrist performs eye exams and prescribes corrective lenses. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Health Care is Teamwork"},{"q":"Which provider assesses, diagnoses, and treats swallowing and fluency disorders?","choices":["Speech-language pathologist","Audiologist and hearing specialist","Occupational therapist","Respiratory care therapist"],"answer":0,"exp":"The speech-language pathologist assesses, diagnoses, and treats swallowing and fluency disorders. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Health Care is Teamwork"},{"q":"A medical lab technologist primarily does what?","choices":["Analyzes body fluids and tissue","Takes and processes diagnostic x-rays","Administers general anesthesia","Provides individual psychotherapy"],"answer":0,"exp":"A medical lab technologist primarily analyzes body fluids and tissue. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Health Care is Teamwork"},{"q":"Which nurse provides anesthesia and requires an RN license plus experience before the program?","choices":["NP","CRNA","CNM","CNS"],"answer":1,"exp":"The CRNA (Certified Registered Nurse Anesthetist) provides anesthesia and requires an RN license plus clinical experience before entering the anesthesia training program. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Health Care is Teamwork"},{"q":"Patient-centered care improves which aspect of care delivery?","choices":["Documentation speed","Cost only","Staffing ratios","Quality of care"],"answer":3,"exp":"Patient-centered care improves the quality of care delivered, consistent with its four tenets of dignity/respect, information sharing, participation, and collaboration. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Health Care is Teamwork"},{"q":"Secondary and tertiary care are distinguished from which level of care?","choices":["Palliative","Emergency","Primary","Hospice"],"answer":2,"exp":"Secondary and tertiary care are distinguished from primary care, which serves as the first point of contact and baseline level of the care hierarchy. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PAs & Clinical Practice"},{"q":"Which is an alternative (non-direct-clinical) role available to PAs?","choices":["Only direct emergency medicine practice","Administration/education/research","Only inpatient surgical practice","Only outpatient primary care practice"],"answer":1,"exp":"Administration, education, and research represent alternative, non-direct-clinical career roles available to PAs beyond patient-facing practice. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — PAs & Clinical Practice"},{"q":"Professionalism, per the Department of Labor context, is needed to succeed and:","choices":["Avoid CME","Retire early","Skip licensure","Move ahead"],"answer":3,"exp":"Professionalism, per the Department of Labor context referenced in the lecture, is needed to succeed and move ahead in one's career. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professionalism"},{"q":"A PA who provides a medical screening exam under EMTALA is performing a function PAs are explicitly permitted to do; PAs may also certify:","choices":["Acute rehab services","Diabetic therapeutic shoes","Terminal illness for hospice","False labor"],"answer":3,"exp":"PAs may certify false labor, one of the functions explicitly permitted alongside performing EMTALA medical screening exams. — Intro to PA Profession lecture — Professional Practice"}]};
